<article class="env-lemma" id="0AGI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AGI">Lemma <span data-tag="0AGI">81.13.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0AGH" data-tag="0AGH">81.13.2</a> let $Y = X' \amalg Z$ and $R = Y \times _ X Y$ with projections $t, s : R \to Y$. There exists a coequalizer $X_1$ of $s, t : R \to Y$ in the category of algebraic spaces over $S$. The morphism $X_1 \to X$ is a finite universal homeomorphism, an isomorphism over $U$, and $Z \to X$ lifts to $X_1$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Existence of $X_1$ and the fact that $X_1 \to X$ is a finite universal homeomorphism is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/0AGG" data-tag="0AGG">81.13.1</a>. The formation of $X_1$ commutes with étale localization on $X$ (see proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0AGG" data-tag="0AGG">81.13.1</a>). Thus the morphism $X_1 \to X$ is an isomorphism over $U$. It is immediate from the construction that $Z \to X$ lifts to $X_1$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>